maya: Quick heads up — opened a tiny PR that consolidates 429/timeouts troubleshooting into a compact runbook. Needs review + sanity check on the SDK snippet and a couple of internal links that 404. PR: https://git.redwood/infer/docs/pull/4823 :wave:

jon: :eyes: Looking. Are the repro steps included in the PR or should we paste them here?

maya: Short repro is in the PR but pasting the minimal steps here so reviewers don't have to click through:
1) Start a dedicated pool, then briefly allow burst to shared.
2) Send ~200 concurrent short requests with batching enabled.
3) Use long conversation prompts so KV cache grows and requests overlap.
Expected: transient 429s and occasional stream interrupts. Observed: sometimes missing Retry-After header on the gateway path.

sam: Good catch. The SDK example in the PR still assumes the old retry header flow. Recommend we show fallback to exponential backoff when header absent. Suggest this small Node snippet instead (paste into the PR):

```js
// minimal client-side retry with fallback to exponential backoff
async function generateWithRetries(client, opts) {
  const max = 5;
  for (let i = 0; i < max; i++) {
    try {
      return await client.generate(opts);
    } catch (err) {
      const retryAfter = err.headers && err.headers['retry-after'];
      if (retryAfter) {
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, Number(retryAfter) * 1000));
      } else {
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, Math.pow(2, i) * 250));
      }
      if (i === max - 1) throw err;
    }
  }
}
```

